From b534ef5476a24118a432bea6a5a7692f50a10d20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 14sea <wanhuaning@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 18 May 2026 22:04:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 3 firmware: epcs_program_page + epcs_erase_sector
 post-op verify
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Closes residual sector-10/12 + page-0 anomaly from patch 0032.

The post-op 4-byte verify (FAST_READ + comparison) serves a dual role:
1. Catches deterministic write corruption per-op (-3 error code).
2. Provides chip-side settling delay between consecutive PP/erase ops
   — without it, sectors 10 and 12 of 0x80000-base writes program
   deterministic-but-wrong content despite chip-side WIP=0 and no
   ILL_* flags.  With it, full 368 KB writes byte-identical.

Empirical path discovered via diagnostic UART trace insertion in
patches/ working branch — the extra FAST_READ calls between PPs
happened to provide the needed inter-op gap.  Converted from debug
form (UART prints) to production form (no prints, -3 error path).

Silicon-validated 2026-05-19:
- mode_t full path: SD SHA OK → idempotent check detects blank slot
  (sha=37b56eeb...) → write_image 368011 B → read-back VERIFY OK
  (sha=6fe90540... matches source).
- External openFPGALoader spiOverJtag dump byte-identical to source.

Stage2 ELF: 22320 → 22456 B (+136 for verify code).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c | 27 +++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 sw/stage2_loader/epcs.h | 17 ++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
index fe9f15d..c5c0f71 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.c
@@ -122,7 +122,18 @@ int epcs_erase_sector(uint32_t addr)
         wait_busy_clear(1000u);
         return -1;
     }
-    return rc == 0 ? 0 : -2;
+    if (rc != 0) return -2;
+
+    /* Post-erase verify (4-byte sample at sector start).  Also serves
+     * as settling delay before the next op — without this gap the next
+     * page program's first byte_valid pulse races with chip-side state
+     * recovery, producing deterministic but wrong content on certain
+     * sector pairs (empirically sectors 10 and 12 in 0x80000-base
+     * writes; silicon-validated 2026-05-19). */
+    uint8_t verify[4];
+    epcs_fast_read(addr, 4, verify);
+    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) if (verify[i] != 0xFFu) return -3;
+    return 0;
 }
 
 int epcs_program_page(uint32_t addr, uint32_t len, const uint8_t *buf)
@@ -182,7 +193,19 @@ int epcs_program_page(uint32_t addr, uint32_t len, const uint8_t *buf)
         wait_busy_clear(1000u);
         return -1;
     }
-    return rc == 0 ? 0 : -2;
+    if (rc != 0) return -2;
+
+    /* Post-PP verify (4-byte sample at page start).  Like the post-
+     * erase verify, this catches deterministic write corruption
+     * empirically observed at scale + provides chip-side settling
+     * delay before the next op (without it, sectors 10 and 12 of
+     * 0x80000-base writes program garbage despite chip-side WIP=0;
+     * with it, full 368 KB writes byte-identical to src). */
+    uint8_t verify[4];
+    uint32_t n = len < 4 ? len : 4;
+    epcs_fast_read(addr, n, verify);
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < n; i++) if (verify[i] != buf[i]) return -3;
+    return 0;
 }
 
 int epcs_write_image(uint32_t base, const uint8_t *src, uint32_t len)
diff --git a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.h b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.h
index 2757811..daeb04b 100644
--- a/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.h
+++ b/sw/stage2_loader/epcs.h
@@ -62,9 +62,10 @@ uint8_t epcs_read_status(void);
 
 /*
  * Erase the 64 KB sector containing addr.  Issues WREN, SEC_ERASE
- * (opcode 0xD8 + 24-bit addr), then polls WIP until clear (tSE max
- * ~3 s per EPCS16 spec).  Returns 0 on success, -1 on illegal_erase
- * sticky, -2 on WIP-poll timeout.
+ * (opcode 0xD8 + 24-bit addr), polls WIP until clear (tSE max ~3 s
+ * per EPCS16 spec), then 4-byte verifies the sector start is 0xff.
+ * Returns 0 on success, -1 on illegal_erase sticky, -2 on WIP-poll
+ * timeout, -3 on post-erase verify mismatch.
  */
 int epcs_erase_sector(uint32_t addr);
 
@@ -72,8 +73,14 @@ int epcs_erase_sector(uint32_t addr);
  * Program up to len bytes (≤ EPCS_PAGE_SIZE) starting at addr.  Caller
  * must ensure (addr & ~(EPCS_PAGE_SIZE-1)) + len-1 stays within the
  * page (the flash wraps within the page silently, which would corrupt
- * data).  Returns 0 on success, -1 on illegal_write sticky, -2 on
- * WIP-poll or DV timeout.
+ * data).  After programming, 4-byte readback verifies the page start
+ * matches buf.  Returns 0 on success, -1 on illegal_write sticky, -2
+ * on WIP-poll or DV timeout, -3 on post-PP verify mismatch.
+ *
+ * Note: the post-PP verify also serves as required chip-side settling
+ * delay before the next op.  Without it, certain sector pairs (sectors
+ * 10 and 12 of 0x80000-base writes) deterministically program wrong
+ * content despite WIP=0 — silicon-validated 2026-05-19.
  */
 int epcs_program_page(uint32_t addr, uint32_t len, const uint8_t *buf);
 
